<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meinwerk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 975–1036</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Meinwerk of Paderborn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meinwerk was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paderborn">Paderborn</a> from 1009 to 1036, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> noble and kinsman of Emperor Henry II. Using his family wealth and imperial grants, he rebuilt the cathedral, founded the Abdinghof monastery and built the Bartholomew Chapel, making Paderborn a major ecclesiastical centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meinwerk.jpg" alt="Meinwerk" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roger of Helmarshausen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FBPB_30_Bischof_Meinwerk_auf_Tragaltar_Helmarshausen_1100.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
